# direnv: auto-enter the pinned toolchain, so the tools you get are the tools
# CI gets. The flake sits at the repo ROOT, which is what lets it see
# `Cargo.toml`/`src/` and offer a real package -- a flake in a subdirectory
# has its own directory as its source root and can offer none.
#
# Entering also puts `rekall` itself on PATH via a `cargo run` shim and `mth`
# via a pinned package, so this crate can check its own spec and its own
# corpus without anyone typing a cargo invocation, and installs the git hooks.
use flake
